    "insert": "The paper presents an innovative and very timely research topic, which explores the potential of holographic AI assistants in educational and workplace settings.\nThe author's motivation is clear, and there seems to be a distinct gap that is addressed with the paper. Furthermore, the motivation is clearly articulated, and examples like Microsoft HoloLens and Apple Vision Pro establish good feasibility and approachability for the concept.\nWhile the overarching and general goal is clear, the paper could benefit from a more explicit main research question and additional, smaller associated sub-research questions. This would provide a stronger focus and help readers—and yourself—understand and distinguish the aim of the paper from other similar studies.\n\nThe chosen mixed-methods approach (combining quantitative experiments and qualitative interviews) seems appropriate and demonstrates a thoughtful strategy. The mention of technological opportunities and ethical challenges shows an understanding of the different areas involved in the topic.\nHowever, especially the experiments could benefit from a short description of how they are supposed to be carried out and how the interviews are then supposed to further benefit the results. \nFurthermore, the tone in parts of the methodology section is overly enthusiastic.\nPhrases like "
